\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {One search, many budgets.} Stage 3: the Stage 2 winner, found once at its natural average budget and rescaled to every target budget with no further search. Stage 4: NAS-refined, the best configuration of the budget-constrained search, available only at budgets where it ran. MOSAIC: its final configuration, the better of Winner and NAS-refined (chosen per budget), at the same budgets as Stage 4. Wins: budgets where the configuration beats uniform on full data; $\Delta $: mean gain over uniform. Llama-3-8B-Instruct; Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2 is in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:app-stages-mistral}.\relax }}{5}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
